; ONMOUSEMOVE: the third background event trigger, alongside ONKEY/
; ONCLICK (see examples/onkey_onclick.logo). Fires on every pointer
; motion over the canvas -- unlike ONCLICK, this can fire dozens of
; times a second, so MOUSEHANDLER below is deliberately cheap (just
; SETXY, no drawing work) to stay smooth. Only makes sense from the
; actual app: the headless test driver has no canvas to ever generate
; a real motion event from.

TO MOUSEHANDLER :X :Y
  SETXY :X :Y
END

PENDOWN
ONMOUSEMOVE "mousehandler

PRINT 'Move the mouse over the canvas -- the turtle follows it, drawing as it goes.'
